# Documents the one variable .env must set. The notebook refuses to start
# without it. Generate a key straight into .env:
#
#   printf 'PII_HMAC_KEY=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" > .env
#
# Secret for the HMAC that tokenises card numbers and transaction ids. There is
# deliberately no default: a key committed to the repository would make every
# token reversible by anyone holding it. Minimum 32 characters.
#
# Rotating it changes every token, which breaks joins to previously published
# extracts — in production the token column needs a version alongside it.
PII_HMAC_KEY=
